(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// Generators (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.4-§7.5; the survey's PYS7 (a); PY5d): a generator, a"] [4 1 "// coroutine and an async generator are the frame of their function's call kept between resumptions."] [5 1 "// The call makes the object without running the frame (newGeneratorHook); each resumption runs the"] [6 1 "// kept frame by (*Thread).run as an entry frame, a yield (yield-value, or yield-from delegating)"] [7 1 "// returns from the loop with Frame.Suspended set, and the frame's handler table sees an exception"] [8 1 "// thrown in at the instruction it is suspended at (Lasti). CPython's Objects/genobject.c and the"] [9 1 "// YIELD_VALUE, SEND and RETURN_GENERATOR parts of Python/bytecodes.c."] [26 1 "// Generator is a generator, a coroutine or an async generator (CPython's PyGenObject, PyCoroObject"] [27 1 "// and PyAsyncGenObject): the kept frame of its function's call."] [30 18 "// nil once finished (gi_frame None)"] [32 18 "// __name__, the function's"] [33 18 "// __qualname__"] [34 18 "// run at least once (FRAME_CREATED otherwise)"] [35 18 "// gi_running"] [36 2 "// handled is the exception the frame is handling while it is suspended (gi_exc_state), nil when none."] [38 2 "// ext is what few generators have, nil until one is set (every generator allocates the rest)"] [40 2 "// the async generator's state (PyAsyncGenObject)"] [41 20 "// ag_closed"] [42 20 "// ag_running_async: an asend or athrow awaits it"] [43 20 "// ag_hooks_inited: sys's firstiter hook called (PY6h's REQUEST, queue 200)"] [44 2 "// finTracked: its finalization is due at its death (finalize.go's workGen, queue 218)"] [46 2 "// finPending: in finalize.go's pendingGens, tracked at the flush when still not finished"] [48 2 "// madeAt, madeF, madeL: callSeq, the calling frame's address and its instruction when made (stampGen; queue 297)"] [52 2 "// exposed: handed out by f_generator (queue 297: then held by more than the value stack)"] [54 2 "// loopHeld: the iterator of the for loop of its making frame, fresh (queue 339: holdLoopGen; closed when the loop pops it)"] [58 1 "// genExt is a generator's rare fields."] [60 2 "// origin is cr_origin: the frames that created a coroutine while origin tracking was on, nil otherwise"] [62 2 "// finalizer is sys's asyncgen finalizer hook at its first use (ag_origin_or_finalizer), nil when none"] [64 2 "// name, qualname: the objects assigned to __name__ and __qualname__, nil until then"] [68 1 "// more is g's rare fields, made when absent."] [86 1 "// newGenerator is a call's object of a function whose code is a generator's, a coroutine's or an"] [87 1 "// async generator's: f bound, not run."] [100 3 "// a coroutine never awaited warns at its death (_PyGen_Finalize; queue 218): tracked only if still not started"] [101 3 "// when the pending list is flushed (most are awaited at once)"] [109 1 "// genThrow is an exception thrown into a suspended frame: the resumption runs the frame's yield-value or yield-from"] [110 1 "// again (its PC set back to Lasti), which finds it here and raises it there, so the frame's handlers see it at the"] [111 1 "// suspension point. Its delegate has had it by then (_gen_throw, throwArgs). One thread runs at a time, and the frame's"] [112 1 "// first instruction run is that one."] [118 1 "// genDone is the outcome of a delegate resume ran itself for a frame suspended at its yield-from (queue 330, passDelegate):"] [119 1 "// the frame goes on from its yield-from, whose instruction finds it here as its send's outcome (what the delegate yielded,"] [120 1 "// returned or raised). One thread runs at a time, and the frame's first instruction run is that one."] [127 1 "// passDelegate is the delegate a resumption of g with a sent value hands the value to without running g's frame (queue 330:"] [128 1 "// CPython's SEND_GEN runs a chain of yield-froms in one loop, pyi's resume ran each level's frame, its loop and its"] [129 1 "// instruction): g's frame suspended at its yield-from on a generator or coroutine, no tool's events, no eval breaker"] [130 1 "// pending, no throw pending for the frame, and the depths below their limits, so that the frame's own resumption would"] [131 1 "// have done nothing before its yield-from sent the value on; nil otherwise."] [145 1 "// genSuspendedAt is the operation f is suspended at, when it is."] [153 1 "// yieldFrom is the delegate the generator is suspended in (gi_yieldfrom), or nil."] [161 1 "// resume runs g with v sent into it (exc nil) or exc raised in it (gen_send_ex2; closing: gen_close's, silent on an"] [162 1 "// exhausted coroutine): the value it yields (yielded non-nil), or the value it returns (returned, the generator"] [163 1 "// finished), or what it raises (err; a StopIteration raised in it is a RuntimeError, PEP 479)."] [182 2 "// a throw nested in this one before its frame took it (a finalizer the frame's start drains closes another"] [183 2 "// generator: queue 297) leaves this one's in place when it is done"] [186 37 "// sent into after a yield (its RESUME's eval breaker raised in it)"] [187 2 "// suspended at a yield-from: RESUME_AFTER_YIELD_FROM checks no eval breaker, the delegate's own resumption does"] [192 4 "// raised at its RESUME: its frame in the traceback, the generator finished"] [208 2 "// the generator's own exception slot over the resuming level's (gi_exc_state pushed on the exc_info stack)"] [219 3 "// queue 330: the value sent on to the delegate here, f entered as run enters it (f_back, the depths, the thread's"] [220 3 "// frame) and running its yield-from (f.PC past it), as its own run would have done before the delegate's"] [232 4 "// the delegate yielded: so does f, from its yield-from (opYieldFrom), as the loop returns a suspended frame"] [240 4 "// the delegate is done (or a tool's events came on): f goes on from its yield-from with that outcome, past its"] [241 4 "// RESUME (it was resumed before the delegate ran)"] [242 24 "// another frame's, should a tool's callback run before f's yield-from took it"] [266 3 "// a generator suspended where a handler can see close()'s GeneratorExit is closed at its death (queue 218)"] [276 15 "// an exhausted generator's frame has no caller"] [284 1 "// stopIterationError is PEP 479's RuntimeError for a StopIteration (or, in an async generator, a"] [285 1 "// StopAsyncIteration) raised out of g's frame: its cause and context the exception, its traceback empty"] [286 1 "// (CPython's INTRINSIC_STOPITERATION_ERROR, re-raised out of the frame)."] [302 2 "// no entry of g's frame (queue 330: CPython's INTRINSIC_STOPITERATION_ERROR makes it in the frame's handler and"] [303 2 "// RERAISE adds none; the StopIteration, its cause, has the frame's)"] [308 1 "// newStopIteration is StopIteration(v), with no arguments when v is None (gen_send_ex's)."] [316 1 "// stopIterationValue is a raised StopIteration's value (_PyGen_FetchStopIterationValue), ok false when"] [317 1 "// err is not one."] [329 1 "// isRaised is err a raised exception of type typ (or a subtype)."] [335 1 "// send is g.send(v): what it yields, or StopIteration with what it returns."] [347 1 "// throwRaised is gen_send_ex with an exception set: err raised in g's frame (a Go error that is no exception as it is)."] [356 1 "// excMatches is PyErr_GivenExceptionMatches of a class or an instance."] [364 1 "// throwArgs is _gen_throw: typ, val and tb as given (nil: not given), first to the delegate; closeOnGenExit false is"] [365 1 "// an async generator's aclose and athrow, whose GeneratorExit is thrown into the delegate. An error in the arguments"] [366 1 "// leaves g suspended."] [385 5 "// the frame linked into the stack, for complete backtraces"] [416 2 "// throw_here"] [441 1 "// normalizeException is PyErr_NormalizeException of a class and a value: the instance, or the exception making it"] [442 1 "// raised (which takes its place)."] [468 1 "// genThrowMethod is gen_throw: the arguments' count and deprecation, then _gen_throw."] [491 1 "// throw is g.throw(...)."] [503 1 "// close is g.close() (gen_close): GeneratorExit thrown in, or what closing its delegate raised; its return value when"] [504 1 "// it returns."] [543 1 "// genSendTo is a send into an iterator delegated to (SEND): a generator's or coroutine's resume, else"] [544 1 "// __next__ when v is None, else its send method; yielded non-nil, or the value it returned (a"] [545 1 "// StopIteration's, or None at an iterator's end)."] [550 40 "// FutureIter_am_send: no StopIteration made"] [554 50 "// PyIter_Send: tp_iternext when it has one"] [556 4 "// a class's __next__ (slot_tp_iternext): its StopIteration's value is the delegate's return (queue 330: the slot"] [557 4 "// ends the for-iter's way, without it)"] [584 1 "// genCloseIter closes a delegate (gen_close_iter): a generator's or coroutine's close, else its close method when it"] [585 1 "// has one."] [603 1 "// asyncGenWrapped is a value an async generator yields (CPython's _PyAsyncGenWrappedValue): its asend"] [604 1 "// and athrow see it apart from the values its awaits yield to the event loop."] [609 1 "// opYieldValue is yield-value: the value popped and yielded (wrapped in an async generator), f kept"] [610 1 "// suspended; resumed, the value sent is on the stack (pushed by resume), or an exception thrown in is"] [611 1 "// raised here."] [627 1 "// chainStackItem is _PyErr_ChainStackItem (gen_send_ex2 with an exception, queue 223): an exception thrown into a"] [628 1 "// generator's frame takes the exception being handled as its __context__ (_PyErr_SetObject's chaining) when the"] [629 1 "// generator's own exception state, pushed at its resumption, holds one."] [638 1 "// opYieldFrom is yield-from ([receiver value] -> its return value): CPython's SEND, YIELD_VALUE and"] [639 1 "// END_SEND loop as one operation. Each value the receiver yields suspends f with the instruction run"] [640 1 "// again on resumption (PC set back to it), the receiver kept below and the sent value pushed on it."] [645 3 "// the delegate resume sent the value to itself (queue 330, passDelegate): its outcome is this send's"] [648 11 "// the placeholder resume pushed"] [658 3 "// CLEANUP_THROW: a StopIteration is the delegate's end, its value this expression's; anything else is raised here"] [661 11 "// the placeholder resume pushed"] [680 54 "// the delegate's end: STOP_ITERATION, or RAISE (queue 219t)"] [691 1 "// opGetYieldFromIter is get-yield-from-iter: a generator or a coroutine as it is (a coroutine only in a"] [692 1 "// coroutine's code), else iter(o)."] [711 1 "// genMethods are the methods of the types of PY5d's files, put into their dictionaries by d5Ready"] [712 1 "// (lazily: a dictionary's keys need str's hash, which str.go's init sets after these files' inits)."] [719 1 "// d5Method declares a method of a type of PY5d's: name in t's dictionary as a built-in method."] [730 1 "// d5Ready fills the dictionaries of PY5d's types with their methods, once (each of their GetAttr"] [731 1 "// slots and operations calls it first)."] [752 1 "// d5GetAttr is the GetAttr slot of PY5d's types: their methods ready, then extra (attributes not in"] [753 1 "// the dictionary), then object's lookup."] [766 1 "// d5Args checks a method's argument count: between min and max positional, no keywords."] [782 1 "// coroOriginDepth is sys.set_coroutine_origin_tracking_depth's depth (0: off)."] [785 1 "// coroOrigin is compute_cr_origin: (filename, lineno, function name) of the creating frame and up to depth-1 of its"] [786 1 "// callers, innermost first."] [802 1 "// genRepr is \"<KIND object QUALNAME at 0x...>\", the address an identity number."] [809 1 "// genGetSets declares the attributes of a generator, coroutine or async generator (prefix gi_, cr_ or ag_; delegate"] [810 1 "// the attribute's name for gi_yieldfrom, cr_await, ag_await)."] [852 40 "// a for loop's get-iter of a fresh generator (queue 339)"] [857 2 "// Next ends without the return value: the loop's for-iter and the abstract Next do not clear a"] [858 2 "// raised StopIteration yet (asked of PY5b and PY5c); __next__ and send raise it with the value."] [893 1 "// asStrSub is a str or a subclass's instance as its Str, else nil."] [901 1 "// nameObj is gi_name: the object set, a str subclass's kept."] [906 2 "// one object each read (gi_name holds it: types.coroutine's wrapper returns gen.__name__ itself, test_types' test_gen)"] [921 1 "// d5GenMethods declares send, throw and close of a generator or a coroutine."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[94 61] [155 38] [204 33] [358 23] [368 24] [380 45] [420 30] [425 25] [427 33] [445 27] [450 28] [457 28] [462 24] [477 145] [515 24] [547 31] [550 33] [555 23] [558 41] [568 44] [573 38] [587 31] [682 42] [695 28] [758 35] [790 18] [790 50] [793 54] [833 37] [852 25] [864 62] [895 30] [924 54] [936 55]]} (go/file "gen.go" :imports [])

;; Generators (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.4-§7.5; the survey's PYS7 (a); PY5d): a generator, a
;; coroutine and an async generator are the frame of their function's call kept between resumptions.
;; The call makes the object without running the frame (newGeneratorHook); each resumption runs the
;; kept frame by (*Thread).run as an entry frame, a yield (yield-value, or yield-from delegating)
;; returns from the loop with Frame.Suspended set, and the frame's handler table sees an exception
;; thrown in at the instruction it is suspended at (Lasti). CPython's Objects/genobject.c and the
;; YIELD_VALUE, SEND and RETURN_GENERATOR parts of Python/bytecodes.c.

